## P1 — Major Usability / Responsive Problems

### 5. MobileBottomNav overlaps page content on small screens
**File**: [MobileBottomNav.tsx](file:///c:/Users/gandh/OneDrive/Desktop/StayEaze/stayeaze-web/src/components/layout/MobileBottomNav.tsx#L46)

The nav has `fixed bottom-0` with `pb-3`, but the main content area in [AppLayout.tsx](file:///c:/Users/gandh/OneDrive/Desktop/StayEaze/stayeaze-web/src/components/layout/AppLayout.tsx#L506) uses `pb-32 md:pb-8`. At 320–480px, `pb-32` (128px) is excessive and wastes valuable vertical space. Meanwhile, at exactly `md` (768px), the nav hides via `md:hidden` but the padding drops to `pb-8` — there's a clean transition. However, the actual nav height is only ~60px, so `pb-32` wastes ~68px of vertical space on mobile.

**Fix**: Reduce to `pb-20 md:pb-8` (80px — enough clearance for the floating nav + safe area insets).

---

### 6. PageHeader actions wrap poorly at 480–767px (phablet range)
**File**: [PageHeader.tsx](file:///c:/Users/gandh/OneDrive/Desktop/StayEaze/stayeaze-web/src/components/common/PageHeader.tsx#L14)

At `sm` (640px), the layout switches to `sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between`. But between 480–639px, the actions `div` uses `flex-wrap` and buttons stack with `gap-2`. This creates a cramped multi-row layout on phablets where buttons are full-width but unnecessarily narrow. 

Many PageHeader consumers pass 2–3 buttons with `flex-1 sm:flex-none` — at 480px, these become equal-width cramped pills.

**Fix**: Keep `flex-col gap-3` below `sm`, then `sm:flex-row`. Add `w-full sm:w-auto` to the actions container for full-width button stacking on mobile.

